{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-72465" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Suppose $B$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix and $det(B)=-2.$ What is the value of $det(3B)?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059016/state.json" "file_sha256" "b8ac332e4afcfb43ecb24854ff19c0fe98e67820fce5e0233dfa8d58d80e25f4"} {"question" "q-72465" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Multiplying a $n\\times n$ matrix by a scalar $k$ is equivalent to multiplying each row by $k,$ and this occurs $n$ times. This leads to the result\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(k\\cdot B)={k}^{n}\\cdot det(B).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $k=3$ and $n=2.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(3B) & ={3}^{2}\\cdot det(B) \\\\  & =9\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =-18.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059016/state.json" "file_sha256" "b8ac332e4afcfb43ecb24854ff19c0fe98e67820fce5e0233dfa8d58d80e25f4"} {"question" "q-72465" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059016/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b04b9a18a4198a7cb601b9689d367a2434fa9d27991a1fd80efa181a6b685909"} {"question" "q-72465" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059016/state.json" "file_sha256" "b8ac332e4afcfb43ecb24854ff19c0fe98e67820fce5e0233dfa8d58d80e25f4"} {"question" "q-72465" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-12"] ["math" "-18"] ["math" "-6"] ["math" "36"] ["math" "54"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059016/state.json" "file_sha256" "b8ac332e4afcfb43ecb24854ff19c0fe98e67820fce5e0233dfa8d58d80e25f4"} {"question" "q-72465" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-18"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059016/state.json" "file_sha256" "b8ac332e4afcfb43ecb24854ff19c0fe98e67820fce5e0233dfa8d58d80e25f4"} {"question" "q-130739" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Suppose $Y$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and $det(Y)=2.$ What is the value of $det(-4Y)?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059016/state.json" "file_sha256" "b8ac332e4afcfb43ecb24854ff19c0fe98e67820fce5e0233dfa8d58d80e25f4"} {"question" "q-130739" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Multiplying a $n\\times n$ matrix by a scalar $k$ is equivalent to multiplying each row by $k,$ and this occurs $n$ times. This leads to the result\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(k\\cdot Y)={k}^{n}\\cdot det(Y).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $k=-4$ and $n=3.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(-4Y) & =(-4)^{3}\\cdot det(Y) \\\\  & =-64\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =-128.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059016/state.json" "file_sha256" "b8ac332e4afcfb43ecb24854ff19c0fe98e67820fce5e0233dfa8d58d80e25f4"} {"question" "q-130739" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059016/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b04b9a18a4198a7cb601b9689d367a2434fa9d27991a1fd80efa181a6b685909"} {"question" "q-130739" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059016/state.json" "file_sha256" "b8ac332e4afcfb43ecb24854ff19c0fe98e67820fce5e0233dfa8d58d80e25f4"} {"question" "q-130739" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-128"] ["math" "-64"] ["math" "-88"] ["math" "160"] ["math" "96"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059016/state.json" "file_sha256" "b8ac332e4afcfb43ecb24854ff19c0fe98e67820fce5e0233dfa8d58d80e25f4"} {"question" "q-130739" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-128"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059016/state.json" "file_sha256" "b8ac332e4afcfb43ecb24854ff19c0fe98e67820fce5e0233dfa8d58d80e25f4"} {"question" "q-130771" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Suppose $B$ is a $6\\times 6$ matrix and $det(B)=-75.$ The matrix $C$ is obtained from $B$ by applying the elementary row operations ${R}_{2}:=\\frac{4}{5}{R}_{2}$ and ${R}_{5}↔{R}_{6}.$ What is the value of $det(C)?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059016/state.json" "file_sha256" "b8ac332e4afcfb43ecb24854ff19c0fe98e67820fce5e0233dfa8d58d80e25f4"} {"question" "q-130771" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's figure out what each operation does to the determinant.\n\n- The operation ${R}_{5}↔{R}_{6}$ involves swapping two rows, so it changes the sign of the determinant to the opposite one.\n\n- The operation ${R}_{2}:=\\frac{4}{5}{R}_{2}$ involves multiplying a row by $\\frac{4}{5},$ so the determinant is multiplied by $\\frac{4}{5}$ as well.\n\nTherefore, we have to change the sign of the determinant to the opposite one and multiply by $\\frac{4}{5}$ as well. Consequently, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(C) & =\\frac{4}{5}\\cdot (-det(B)) \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{5}det(B) \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{5}\\cdot (-75) \\\\  & =60.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059016/state.json" "file_sha256" "b8ac332e4afcfb43ecb24854ff19c0fe98e67820fce5e0233dfa8d58d80e25f4"} {"question" "q-130771" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059016/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b04b9a18a4198a7cb601b9689d367a2434fa9d27991a1fd80efa181a6b685909"} {"question" "q-130771" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059016/state.json" "file_sha256" "b8ac332e4afcfb43ecb24854ff19c0fe98e67820fce5e0233dfa8d58d80e25f4"} {"question" "q-130771" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-75"] ["math" "-90"] ["math" "40"] ["math" "60"] ["math" "90"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059016/state.json" "file_sha256" "b8ac332e4afcfb43ecb24854ff19c0fe98e67820fce5e0233dfa8d58d80e25f4"} {"question" "q-130771" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "60"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059016/state.json" "file_sha256" "b8ac332e4afcfb43ecb24854ff19c0fe98e67820fce5e0233dfa8d58d80e25f4"} {"question" "q-130855" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the matrices given below. Given that $X$ and $Y$ are row equivalent matrices and $det(X)=5$, find $det(Y).$\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 2 & 2\\end{aligned}],\\,Y=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059016/state.json" "file_sha256" "b8ac332e4afcfb43ecb24854ff19c0fe98e67820fce5e0233dfa8d58d80e25f4"} {"question" "q-130855" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that $Y$ can be obtained from $X$ by swapping the $2$nd and the $3$rd rows. \n\nThis changes the sign of the determinant to the opposite one.\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(Y) & =-det(X) \\\\  & =-(5) \\\\  & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059016/state.json" "file_sha256" "b8ac332e4afcfb43ecb24854ff19c0fe98e67820fce5e0233dfa8d58d80e25f4"} {"question" "q-130855" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059016/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b04b9a18a4198a7cb601b9689d367a2434fa9d27991a1fd80efa181a6b685909"} {"question" "q-130855" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059016/state.json" "file_sha256" "b8ac332e4afcfb43ecb24854ff19c0fe98e67820fce5e0233dfa8d58d80e25f4"} {"question" "q-130855" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-10"] ["math" "-15"] ["math" "-5"] ["math" "10"] ["math" "5"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059016/state.json" "file_sha256" "b8ac332e4afcfb43ecb24854ff19c0fe98e67820fce5e0233dfa8d58d80e25f4"} {"question" "q-130855" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-5"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059016/state.json" "file_sha256" "b8ac332e4afcfb43ecb24854ff19c0fe98e67820fce5e0233dfa8d58d80e25f4"} {"question" "q-130857" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the matrices given below. Given that $X$ and $Y$ are row equivalent matrices and $det(X)=-60$, find $det(Y).$\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}],\\,Y=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -3\\end{aligned}]?\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059016/state.json" "file_sha256" "b8ac332e4afcfb43ecb24854ff19c0fe98e67820fce5e0233dfa8d58d80e25f4"} {"question" "q-130857" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that $Y$ can be obtained from $X$ by swapping the $1$st and the $3$rd rows. \n\nThis changes the sign of the determinant to the opposite one.\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(Y) & =-det(X) \\\\  & =-(-60) \\\\  & =60.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059016/state.json" "file_sha256" "b8ac332e4afcfb43ecb24854ff19c0fe98e67820fce5e0233dfa8d58d80e25f4"} {"question" "q-130857" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059016/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b04b9a18a4198a7cb601b9689d367a2434fa9d27991a1fd80efa181a6b685909"} {"question" "q-130857" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059016/state.json" "file_sha256" "b8ac332e4afcfb43ecb24854ff19c0fe98e67820fce5e0233dfa8d58d80e25f4"} {"question" "q-130857" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-50"] ["math" "-60"] ["math" "50"] ["math" "60"] ["math" "96"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059016/state.json" "file_sha256" "b8ac332e4afcfb43ecb24854ff19c0fe98e67820fce5e0233dfa8d58d80e25f4"} {"question" "q-130857" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "60"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059016/state.json" "file_sha256" "b8ac332e4afcfb43ecb24854ff19c0fe98e67820fce5e0233dfa8d58d80e25f4"}] "usage" {"q-72465" []} "basis" 1886 "retractions" [[17592186120440 :question/problem "Suppose $B$ is a $2 \\cdot 2$ matrix and $det(B) =-2$. What is the value of $det(3B)$?"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186119116 17592186119117 17592186119118 17592186119119 17592186119120] "immutable_fields" [[17592186119115 :answer-field/correct] [17592186119115 :answer-field/id] [17592186119115 :answer-field/key] [17592186119115 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
